## Methods and QC decisions
- Continued using the fixed pre-QC pipeline: raw FIF conversion, event-based epoching from `STI101_up`, baseline correction from -100 to 0 ms, downsampling to 200 Hz, high-pass filtering at 0.5 Hz, and low-pass filtering at 20 Hz.
- Initial bad channels were selected only when a channel appeared repeatedly across the structured trial sample and across more than one condition type.
- Bad channels were saved using index-based SPM marking to avoid the earlier issue where all MEG channels could be accidentally marked bad.
- Participant-specific artefact thresholds were selected from the approximate 97.5th percentile of maximum absolute trial amplitude across currently good MEG channels. This produced approximately 2.5% trial rejection per participant.
- Robust averaging was run by condition using `ks = 3`, `bycondition = 1`, `savew = 1`, and `removebad = 1`.
- Ranked-channel QC was used after averaging whenever visual inspection suggested a possible remaining rogue channel. Additional channels were added only when clearly justified.
- Averaged condition order was explicitly checked for each participant rather than assumed. This was important for `sub-2269A`, where the averaged order was Standard, Duration Deviant, Pitch Deviant.

